=== rtph264pay actual property defaults (gst-inspect-1.0 on this machine) ===
config-interval: our code sets =1 -- "Send SPS and PPS Insertion Interval in seconds (sprop parameter sets will
                 be multiplexed in the data stream when detected.)" -- CONFIRMS this delivers SPS/PPS IN-BAND
                 in the RTP stream (matches Step 3's finding: no out-of-band sprop-parameter-sets in the SDP,
                 because this mechanism doesn't populate SDP -- it inserts SPS/PPS as in-band NAL units before
                 IDR frames instead).
pt:              our code sets =96 (matches SDP payload type 96, Step 3, confirmed consistent)
timestamp mode:  perfect-rtptime -- library default (true), our code does not override it. Correct for a live
                 encoder source; not an interop concern.
seqnum-offset / timestamp-offset: library defaults (random) -- normal for a live stream.
